  "taxResidenceDefault": "Calculated with Bizkaia's rules. You can change your tax residence in Settings.",
  "taxHowIntroComun": "Under the Spanish personal income tax law, Ley 35/2006, common regime.",
  "taxHowWashBodyComun": "If you sell stocks or ETFs at a loss and buy the same in the two months before or after, that loss waits until you sell what you bought back. Crypto has no such rule: the loss counts in full.",
  "taxHowSwapSourceComun": "Art. 37.1.h",
  "taxHowIncomeTitleComun": "Income and gains offset each other",
  "taxHowIncomeBodyComun": "Interest and dividends form their own pool. One pool's negative balance offsets the other's positive one up to 25% of it, and so do earlier years' pending losses its own pool does not absorb, within one limit a year. The savings base adds the positive balances of both pools.",
  "taxHowRulesComun": "The same sales, on a FIFO basis instead of AVCO, which is what income tax (Ley 35/2006) requires and not what the Sales tab uses; for crypto, FIFO per asset (DGT V1604-18 and V0975-22). A loss on a stock or ETF with a repurchase in the two months before or after does not compute under art. 33.5.f, in the proportion repurchased, and computes when the repurchased units are transmitted. That is the rule for securities admitted to trading on a regulated EEA market or an equivalent one (the US included, DGT V0778-25); those not admitted have one year (art. 33.5.g), and Quoin does not know which market each security trades on. Crypto has no repurchase rule: its loss counts in full. Swaps are valued at the greater of the two values (art. 37.1.h, DGT V0999-18). Offsetting between the pools and against earlier years follows art. 49. The repurchase arithmetic follows the DGT rulings V1403-21, V1117-21 and V3282-18.",
  "taxUnlistedReasonComun": "Crypto sold at a loss and bought again on {date}. The common regime has no specific repurchase rule for crypto assets. Art. 33.5.e (repurchase of the same asset within the following year) could apply, but the DGT has not settled it. Quoin does not defer the loss: it counts in full.",
  "taxScaleSource": "Scale applied: {source}.",
  "taxPoolsComun": "Income from movable capital and capital gains and losses are each integrated in their own pool. One pool's negative balance offsets the other's positive one up to 25% of it, and so do earlier years' pending losses its own pool does not absorb, within the same 25% for the whole year: the base is the sum of the positive balances.",
  "taxIncomeBodyComun": "Interest and dividends paid in cash, and Trade Republic's saveback, which the broker declares as account income. Gross amounts. A negative balance offsets capital gains up to 25% of their positive balance, and what is left is carried to the following years.",
  "taxCrossOffset": "Offset within the year",
  "taxCrossFromEarlier": "From the other pool, earlier years",
  "taxPools": "Income from movable capital and capital gains and losses compensate only within their own pool: the base is the sum of the positive balances.",
  "taxWithheld": "Recorded withholdings",
  "taxWithheldNote": "Withholdings are payments on account of the whole income tax, not only of the savings base, and are not subtracted from the tax. This adds up what was withheld this year on interest and dividends paid in cash and on Trade Republic's saveback, with no split between Spanish and foreign withholdings.",
  "taxInterestWithoutWithholding": "Some interest this year has no recorded withholding. Interest imported before this version may lack its withholding even if it had one: check it against the broker's statement.",
  "taxScaleInForce": "The {territory} scale in force since {year} applies. If a new one is approved for this year, the tax will change.",
  "taxIncomeTitle": "Income from movable capital",
  "taxIncomeBody": "Interest and dividends paid in cash, and Trade Republic's saveback, which the broker declares as account income. Gross amounts. They compensate only among themselves, and a negative balance is carried to the following years.",
